This repository is a *mixed-licence* tree by design. The Apache-2.0 licence
above covers the hardware-agnostic core: build tooling, board-profile schema,
CI checks, provisioning and fleet scripts. Components with a different licence
carry it in their own directory, and their licence governs there:

  boards/**/kernel.yaml, bsp/**    Linux kernel and U-Boot are GPL-2.0. Our
                                   config fragments and patches to them are
                                   GPL-2.0 as derived works. Shipping a kernel
                                   binary obliges us to provide the complete
                                   corresponding source to whoever receives the
                                   device — see docs/gpl-compliance.md.

  apps/openems/bundles/**          OpenEMS device drivers are EPL-2.0, matching
                                   upstream OpenEMS Edge, so they can be
                                   contributed upstream. EPL-2.0 is weak,
                                   file-level copyleft; it does not reach the
                                   Apache-2.0 core.

Not redistributed here, and deliberately absent:

  Rockchip loader binaries (rk3576_spl_loader, rk3576_idblock) are proprietary
  vendor blobs under Rockchip's own terms. They are fetched at build time from
  the vendor delivery, never committed.

  Board vendor documentation, schematics and mechanical files are the vendor's
  copyright and are not redistributable. Facts derived from them (port counts,
  device-tree node names) are recorded in board profiles with attribution;
  the source documents are not included.
